Z||000002||kslish||06-09-2001||07:03 PM||||Where does this guy work and are they hiring?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Speaking of nifty cars though, it seems the weather has finally become nice enough (i.e. no rain) to bring out the nice cars here in Western PA for the summer.  Just driving to the bank yesterday I saw a couple new Vettes, a Viper roadster and a fairly new bright red Lotus Esprit (probably the only exotic car I plan to own some day...they are somewhat common here and you can pick up one of the older 4-cyl turbo ones for around $15K-$20K with around 35,000 miles on it).  This Esprit had the V8 though so I had to drool a little.<P>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||06-09-2001||09:50 PM||||Dude in my previous post is my new neighbor. He's a wine salesman, but must be doing very well.<P>Beautiful weather today. Lots o' people getting the cars out. Some of the less common ones I see were: three Prowlers(2 purple, 1 yellow), couple ZO6s, another Bullit Mustang, different neighbor took his Pantera out for a few laps around the block. I was helping a friend move out of his apartment, so I only got to see the streets a couple of times today. <BR>BTW, while helping my friend move, we decided to race an Avenger with his loaded to the top with crap to move '88 Celica. By the time 60mph came up, we were a car length ahead <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Both were autos, thought it was pretty funny to see the other driver wondering how that POS Celica was beating him.||||reg||1
